qa+=['','## Measurement and universe','The five items PES5A–PES5E were independently verified against the official 2013 questionnaire, codebook, API metadata and released raw layout. Any observed Yes classifies S2=1. All five No classifies S2=0. Otherwise the respondent is excluded from the valid denominator. NIU, refused, DK and missing are never recoded as No. PES7 measures leadership and is not a sixth organizational type.','Operational eligibility: civilian noninstitutional household persons age 18+, PRPERTYP=2, PRSUPINT=1, positive PWNRWGT. Self or proxy response is permitted; the reporting household member must be age 18+.','UNKNOWN — DOCUMENT/RAW CONFLICT: Attachment 1 says outgoing rotation households. Attachment 3 specifies MIS 3,4,7,8. Released eligible records occur only in MIS 3=9776, 4=9466, 7=9481, 8=9878. Canonical estimates retain all officially released eligible supplement interviews. These reproduce official PES5A frequencies and national item totals. IPUMS 2013 group-item documentation independently supports MIS 3,4,7,8, but does not erase the Census contradiction.','Attachment 7 also lists an upstream PES3 restriction inconsistent with released frequency responses 3–6. The officially edited group responses are retained; no additional upstream filter is invented. The dictionary preserves this discrepancy.','','## Replicate-weight verification','The official 2013 Census page supplies the nonresponse replicate file and links person-level supplement instructions. The 2013 data, SAS layout and linked instructions were downloaded independently. There are 160 replicates plus full-sample weight 0, with four implied decimal places. The instructions expressly specify variance=(4/160)*sum((replicate estimate-full estimate)^2). Their March 7, 2012 date and applicability to CPS person-level supplements are recorded; the URL directory 2018 is only the hosting location.','QSTNUM/OCCURNUM merges are one-to-one. Repwgt0 matches PWNRWGT for all 38601 eligible people. All 161 published column totals match exactly. Each replicate recomputes both weighted Yes and the valid-response denominator. Saved replicate estimates independently reproduce all 50 state SEs.','The 2013 SAS starts fields 39 and 69 one character late. Parsing contiguous ten-character blocks is validated against every published column total and each person’s full-sample weight. No unverified formula from 2011, S3 or another year is applied.','','## API and source QA','API metadata was successfully downloaded. All five public weighted queries returned non-JSON Missing Key pages. No Census secret was available in the execution environment. API weighted comparison: NOT COMPLETED — UNAVAILABLE_AUTH_REQUIRED. No API count agreement is claimed.','Attempt 1 exited with code 2 at the API availability gate. The final implementation records technical unavailability under the directive’s “where technically available” condition. Attempt 1 code, log and checks are preserved. The pre-execution QA specification hash and numerical thresholds did not change.','Census Attachment 13 PES5A frequencies match exactly. Attachment 16 school and sports weighted Yes totals match within the predeclared 500-person published-rounding tolerance. The published population base is reproduced using basic PWSSWGT over adult civilians; it is not substituted for the canonical valid-response union denominator.','','## Independent external benchmark','FOUND: the 2015 North Carolina Civic Health Index explicitly identifies 2013 CPS November Civic Engagement as the data source for its any-organization rates (report pages 14,17,37). Its missing-response algorithm is not specified. Differences are diagnostic and retained; published values are never copied into canonical estimates. The 0.05 percentage-point rounding tolerance was fixed before execution.']
